pd-score-corpus
===============

This project is a curated *subset selector* for PDMX. It is not affiliated
with the PDMX authors, UC San Diego, MuseScore, Ultimate Guitar, or
Creative Commons.

PDMX
----

PDMX: A Large-Scale Public Domain MusicXML Dataset for Symbolic Music
Processing, by Phillip Long, Zachary Novack, Julian McAuley, and
Taylor Berg-Kirkpatrick.

- Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.10831
- HTML (v2): https://arxiv.org/html/2409.10831v2
- Dataset (Zenodo v9, 1 June 2025): https://zenodo.org/records/15571083
  DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.15571083
  Concept DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.13763755
- Code (MIT License, Copyright 2023 Phillip Long): https://github.com/pnlong/PDMX
- Demo: https://pnlong.github.io/PDMX.demo/

PDMX authors request that users of the dataset also cite Xu, McAuley,
Berg-Kirkpatrick, Dubnov, and Dong, "Generating Symbolic Music from Natural
Language Prompts using an LLM-Enhanced Dataset" (MetaScore),
arXiv:2410.02084. They thank Hao-Wen Dong for scraping MuseScore and
compiling the source data used to create PDMX.

The PDMX *code* is MIT-licensed. The PDMX *dataset compilation* is described
by the authors as CC-BY (Zenodo record license: CC-BY-4.0). Individual score
encodings in PDMX were selected from MuseScore.com rows whose uploaders
declared CC0 or Public Domain Mark.

PDMX authors later reported a discrepancy between MuseScore's public-facing
copyright metadata and the internal copyright field of the MuseScore files
themselves, affecting 31,221 songs (12.29%). They recommend the
`no_license_conflict` subset (222,856 songs). This project's filter requires
that subset.

MuseScore encodings
-------------------

Score files originated as user uploads on MuseScore.com. This repository
does not scrape MuseScore. It redistributes a *curated subset derived from
the Zenodo dump of PDMX*. MuseScore Terms of Use restrict scraping and
redistribution of content downloaded from MuseScore.com itself; the
relationship between those terms and a third-party Zenodo dump is uncertain
and is flagged in LEGAL.md. This project is not affiliated with MuseScore.

Do not assume any file is "cleared for film." See LEGAL.md.
